  "body": "## This relates to...\n\nFixes #5974\n\n## Rationale\n\nWhen several requests for the same hostname arrive before its DNS entry is cached, each one started its own lookup. A burst of concurrent requests to a cold hostname therefore triggered one resolver lookup per request instead of one for the group.\n\n## Changes\n\n`runLookup` now records an in-flight lookup in a `#pendingLookups` map keyed by the hostname plus the resolution-affecting options (`affinity`, `dualStack`). A request that finds a pending entry for its key is added to that entry's waiter list instead of starting a lookup of its own; otherwise it starts one and registers itself as the first waiter. When the lookup completes, every waiter runs the existing `pick` logic against the shared records, so each request still selects its own address and the per-request origin, port, protocol, and round-robin behavior are unchanged. The pending entry is removed before the result is fanned out, so a failed lookup is reported to all attached waiters and a later request for the same hostname starts a fresh lookup.\n\nA regression test in `test/issue-5974.js` covers a cold-cache burst performing a single lookup (and a warm burst performing none), concurrent waiters picking addresses independently from the shared lookup, and a failing lookup being shared while its pending state is cleared so the next request retries. `npm run lint`, `npm run test:interceptors` (446 pass / 0 fail) and `npm run test:unit` (1613 pass / 0 fail) pass.\n\n### Features\n\nN/A\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Concurrent requests for the same cold hostname now share a single DNS lookup instead of each starting their own. (Fixes #5974)\n\n### Breaking Changes and Deprecations\n\nN/A\n\n## Status\n\n<!-- KEY: S = Skipped, x = complete -->\n\n\n- [x] I have read and agreed to the [Developer's Certificate of Origin][cert]\n- [x] Tested\n- [ ] Benchmarked (**optional**)\n- [x] Documented\n- [x] Review ready\n- [ ] In review\n- [ ] Merge ready\n\n[cert]: https://github.com/nodejs/undici/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#developers-certificate-of-origin\n\n",
